{"text": "G/WICK BUSINESS CENTRE TEL No.0293-S67S02 30 Mar 92 1\n\n117 No.002 P.O1\n\n\u2018Eingegangen\nTelefax Copy #5086 sami992\n\nMarch 30, 1992\n\natta Dr Reininghaus/ Dr Hackenberg\n\nGood morning,\n\nSince my last visit to Inbifo I have tried to obtain information on\ntesting of products which are not pharmacological drugs but expose\nbody surfaces to active ingredients.\n\nTelephone calls have been made to our Government Bureau of Toxic\nsubstances Stockholm, the Institue of Pharmaceutical Druge Uppsala and\nthe department of Skin diseases in Gothenburg.\n\nThe picure that emerges is reasonably clear. If the substance to be\ntested is intended to alter any function of the body for therapeutic\nuse, it is classified as a drug and should be tested like one. There\nis a number of what is called \u201cnatural substances\" (ging-seng etc)\nwhich can be used after formal registration only.\n\nFor other substances, they cannot contain substances which are known\nto be toxic e.g. bensene, chloroform. Otherwise there are no\nparticular rules to follow - the person handling, selling and\ndistributing, the substance has the responsibility that it does not\ncontain any harmful agents.\n\nIn all types of testing which is done by phycisians, approval of the\nethical committee is required. The test persons informed consent is\nrequired (although not in written form ag in the States) and he/she\nhas the possibility to terminate the test whenever he/she wants\n\n1 hope that the above is of some help. 1f you need to contact me 1 am\n\nat the Sterling Hotel, Gatwick tel +44 293 567070 or fax +44 293\n567739 room 892 till Wednesday.\n\nWith my kindest regards\n\nRagnar Rylander\n\nbEEz0N9zZ0z",
